==English==

===Etymology===
The English surname Neave was brought to England in the {{w|Norman Conquest}} of 1066. It is derived from the {{der|en|fro|neveu||[[nephew]]}}. {{w|William the Conquerer}} granted lands to many Norman [[Baron]]s, and the Neave family is thought to be descended from one of these Barons.

